  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public health law, in relation to the New York state adult\ncystic fibrosis program; and to amend a chapter of the laws of 2023, amending\nthe public health law relating to the adult cystic fibrosis assistance\nprogram, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 6521 and A. 3089, in\nrelation to the effectiveness thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S8002",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8002-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §2795, Pub Health L; amd §2, Chap of 2023 (as proposed in S.6521 & A.3089)",
    "lawSection": "Public Health Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8002\n\nSPONSOR: THOMAS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public health law, in relation to the New York state\nadult cystic fibrosis program; and to amend a chapter of the laws of\n2023, amending the public health law relating to the adult cystic fibro-\nsis assistance program, as proposed in legislative bills numbers S. 6521\nand A. 3089, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nThis is a chapter amendment that makes changes to provisions of\nL.2023,c.769, to clarify provisions relating to the implementation of\nthe Adult Cystic Fibrosis Assistance Program\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis underlying chapter directs the Department of Health to create the\nAdult Cystic Fibrosis Assistance program to provide financial support to\nadults with cystic fibrosis who are underinsured and need assistance\naccessing needed services for the treatment of their condition. This\nlegislation amends this chapter by codifying the program as it currently\noperates rather than to re-establish the program as it existed prior to\nits repeal in 2020.\n\nThe Health Commissioner is authorized to enter into a contract with a\nthird-party administrator to operate this program through March 31,\n2024.\n\nThe legislation also sets eligibility criteria and increases the\nreimbursement to ensure individuals receive full reimbursement for the\nservice or treatment not covered rather than limit to the Medicaid rate.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation is a negotiated change to the underlying chapter.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nChapter amendment to Chapter 769 of the Laws of 2023. S.6521 and A.3089\nboth passed the Senate and Assembly, respectfully, in June 2023.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNo fiscal.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately; provided, however, that section\none of this act shall take effect on the same date and in the same\nmanner as a chapter of the laws of 2023 amending the public health law\nrelating to the adult cystic fibrosis assistance program, as proposed in\nlegislative bills numbers S. 6521 and A. 3089, takes effect; provided,\nfurther, that the amendments to section 2795 of the public health law\nmade by section one of this act shall not affect the repeal of such\nsection and shall be deemed repealed therewith.\n",
